// endpoint_report_user_interaction.proto — ReportUserInteraction: the user
// interacted with this workspace. HOST section.
//
// THE ONE INPUT TO VIEWED AND TO RECENCY. A workspace is viewed exactly when
// the user has interacted with it since its status last changed, and the
// recency walk orders workspaces by when the user last interacted with each.
// The daemon derives both from this report alone
// (frontend.v1.RosterRowViewed, frontend.v1.RosterRowLastInteracted); a
// client reports the fact and decides neither.
//
// ONLY THE USER'S OWN ACTS ARE REPORTED. A scroll the page makes itself
// (following new output, revealing a row, a jump), text the editor inserts
// itself (a restored draft, a completion's fill), and a switch to the
// workspace are no interaction, and a client never reports them. Looking at a
// workspace for any length of time is not an interaction either: there is no
// dwell.
//
// TWO SENDERS. The page that draws the workspace's feed reports the reader's
// own scrolling of it; the editor reports typing in the workspace's composer
// and moving through its feed with the editor's keys. A link the reader
// follows in the page needs no report: the daemon receives the click itself
// (OpenExternal, OpenInEditor, SelectInEditor's `followed_from`) and records
// it as an interaction there.
//
// IDEMPOTENT, and cheap to repeat: an interaction with a workspace that is
// already viewed and already the most recent re-stamps its instant and
// changes nothing a client draws. A sender still coalesces a burst (one
// report per gesture, not per wheel event).

